  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>Tahuantinsuyoa macantzatza, the Inca Stone Fish, reaches a maximum length of 12 cm when fully grown. Origin: Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>After fearing for years that the species had become extinct, a larger number of them was imported at the beginning of 2003. Both wild-caught fish and captive-bred fish are now available.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>Because the fish reach a full-grown length of at most 12 cm, they are suitable for medium-sized aquariums.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>The water should not be too hard and should have a slightly acidic tendency.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>They do not damage plants, so they can be kept in tanks decorated with bogwood and plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>There are no special requirements for feeding.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/tahuantinsuyoa_macantzatza_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are larvophile mouthbrooders: the eggs are laid and kept first on a substrate, then the larvae are protected in the mouth. The transfer of the fry between the parents is always exciting to observe.</p>"
    }
  ],
